        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.447,
          "end": 4.819,
          "en": "Speaker: That was a lot of talking about observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.819,
          "end": 6.267,
          "en": "but now we have an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.267,
          "end": 10.17,
          "en": "of an observable and how it behaves under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.17,
          "end": 12.99,
          "en": "However, I know that this can look even more confusing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.99,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "and you might ask yourself, well, when do I write this code?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "Because that's nice about the interval, but come on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "I don't need that interval that often in my application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "And you would be right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 25.53,
          "en": "And by the way, if you needed one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.53,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "you'd of course use the built-in interval function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 29.34,
          "en": "and not build your own one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 31.097,
          "en": "So, what's the idea behind that example?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.097,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "The idea is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "that you understand what happens inside of an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 38.19,
          "en": "Whenever you subscribe, and you set-up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.19,
          "end": 41.73,
          "en": "your different handler functions here, our xjs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.73,
          "end": 43.453,
          "en": "in the end merges them all together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.453,
          "end": 47.184,
          "en": "into one object and passes that object, the observer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.184,
          "end": 49.89,
          "en": "to the observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.89,
          "end": 51.231,
          "en": "And inside of the observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.231,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "it will then interact with the observer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "and let the observer know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 57.93,
          "en": "about new data and errors and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 60,
          "en": "And that is how your functions get called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 62.61,
          "en": "However, you rarely very, very",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.61,
          "end": 65.919,
          "en": "very rarely build your own observables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 65.919,
          "end": 66.836,
          "en": "More often,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 66.836,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "you use observables that come with libraries, like angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.68,
          "end": 73.38,
          "en": "like the route parents observable we already used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 73.38,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 75.173,
          "en": "That in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 75.173,
          "end": 78.09,
          "en": "is a custom observable built by the angular team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 80.444,
          "en": "But of course, you just use it like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 80.444,
          "end": 82.092,
          "en": "You rarely build your own ones,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 82.092,
          "end": 83.902,
          "en": "but still it's super important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 83.902,
          "end": 86.78999999999999,
          "en": "to understand how they work under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 86.78999999999999,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "And in the end, they all work a bit like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 91.95,
          "en": "They wrap some event source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 91.95,
          "end": 93.638,
          "en": "In this case it's set interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 93.638,
          "end": 95.89699999999999,
          "en": "In our cases it could be an AJAX request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 95.89699999999999,
          "end": 99.205,
          "en": "or a click listener or whatever it is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 99.205,
          "end": 101.16,
          "en": "and they give you data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
